Recommends: quota
Description: cluster-wide user and access management from one file
 grantctl manages Linux accounts, SSH access, sudo rights and resource limits
 across a small Debian/Ubuntu cluster from a single source-of-truth file.
 .
 Each user is one line in access.conf, listing roles such as admin, student
 or gpu, optionally scoped to nodes. grantctl runs on a control node and
 reaches the other nodes over SSH; there is no daemon. On every node it
 creates missing accounts, keeps group membership exact, writes its own
 sshd_config.d, sudoers.d and limits.d files, and applies per-user slice
 limits and disk quotas.
 .
 Changes are validated with visudo and sshd -t, backed up, and rolled back
 on failure; access is only removed after the new rules are live.
 .
 Install this package on the control node and on every managed node.
